    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0132" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.24/563: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-06T09:00:00+02:00">February 6, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>193. We learned last night from a source which we consider thoroughly reliable
                    that the French Government has entered into some form of accord with the Axis
                    Powers whereby French ships are being used for the transport of munitions and
                    supplies from France to Tunis, presumably destined for Rommel’s<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d135-f1"/> forces in Libya.</p>
                <p>We expect to obtain further information on this matter today. The Department’s
                    attention is invited in this respect to telegram no. 192, February 6, 9
                        a.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d135-f2"/> from our Naval Attaché.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d135-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to London and Casablanca for Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d135-f1" n="12" xml:id="d135-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Erwin Rommel, Commander of German Forces in Libya.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d135-f2" n="13" xml:id="d135-f2-content">
